## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of per-tenant feature flags and zero-downtime rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes ConfigMaps and pod configuration propagation
- Environment variables vs mounted files for configuration delivery
- Canary deployments and rollback safety mechanisms
- Observability practices and latency budget management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Reads a per-tenant flag from environment variable with fallback to false
function isBetaEnabled(tenantId){
  const cfg = JSON.parse(process.env.TENANT_FLAGS || '{}');
  return !!cfg[tenantId]?.betaRoute;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of network policies and safe rollback in a novice-friendly way. It emphasizes isolating networking changes, validating through pod-level checks, and ensuring performance targets during recovery.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes NetworkPolicy egress rules
- In-cluster vs external services
- kubectl exploration and testing
- Zero-downtime rollback and load testing
- Latency targets (P95) during recovery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple latency check (pseudo)
async function measure(url){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(url);
  return performance.now() - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
